<title>TURKEY: Turkish C/A deficit rises to $138 mln in February.</title>
<headline>Turkish C/A deficit rises to $138 mln in February.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's current account deficit rose to $138 million in February from $21 million in the same 1995 month, the central bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>			  Feb95   Feb96 Jan-Feb95 Jan-Feb96</p>
<p> Current Account	 -21    -138    587	  151</p>
<p> Exports FOB	   1,586   1,697  3,155	3,465</p>
<p> Imports FOB	  -2,204  -2,746 -4,213     -5,667</p>
<p> Gold Imports	   -28     -92    -48	 -149</p>
<p> Foreign trade blnc   -618  -1,153 -1,058     -2,202</p>
<p> Invisible credit	941   1,268  1,816	2,978</p>
<p> Tourism		  154     175    318	  348</p>
<p> Invisible Debit	-677    -790 -1,248     -1,531</p>
<p> Interest payment    -325    -335   -539	 -610</p>
<p> Transfers from abroad 289     303    519	  726</p>
<p> Capital account     1,231     350  2,034	1,650</p>
<p> Overall Balance     1,349     573  3,412	2,182</p>
